  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="ilpas-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אילפס</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾylps</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">ʾilpas</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa">אלפס</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">ʾlps</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic">ʾilpas</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <form type="inflected">
               <orth type="inflected" xml:lang="jpa">אילפסין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">ʾylpsyn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">ʾilpasin</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="ilpas-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>covered pot</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>λοπάς</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>אמר ר' שמעון תמיה אני היך נחלקו אבות העולם בדבר זה שלא נבראו אלא שניהם 
                     <app>
                        <lem>כאילפס</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1 V">אלפס</rdg>
                     </app> וכיסויה קורא אני אליהם יעמדו יחדיו</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">1,15</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 14: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Shimʿon said: I wonder how the fathers of the world (i.e. the rabbis) had a controversy on this matter, for both (i.e. the sky and the earth) were create (together) like a pot and it’s cover, (as it is written:) When I call unto them, they stand up together (Jes 48,13).</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Gen 4 [2c: 27]</bibl></note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Frequently attested in rabbinic literature (e.g. <bibl type="ancient">mShab 3,5</bibl>; <bibl type="ancient">tNed 3,1</bibl>; <bibl type="ancient">bEr 53b</bibl>). Jastrow leads back to the root <term xml:lang="fjb">lps</term> (reject). Pl. is not attested in GenR.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Heijmans 2013</title>
                  <citedRange>126</citedRange>
               </bibl>
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>57-58</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
